        "original_id": "e1566261-4008-5c4a-94ef-756b716e3ad3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alessandro Scarlatti, Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky\n- Roles: composers\n- Topics: Baroque music, Romantic period, opera, chamber cantatas, classical repertoire, international recognition\n\nFacts:\n- Alessandro Scarlatti was born on 2 May 1660 and died on 22 October 1725.\n- Alessandro Scarlatti was an Italian Baroque composer especially famous for his operas and chamber cantatas.\n- Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky was born on 25 April/7 May 1840 and died on 25 October/6 November 1893.\n- Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky, often anglicized as Peter Ilich Tchaikovsky, was a Russian composer of the Romantic period.\n- Some works by Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky are among the most popular music in the classical repertoire.\n- Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky was the first Russian composer whose music made a lasting international impression.\n- Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky's international recognition was bolstered by his appearances as a guest conductor in Europe and the United States.",
